{
  "_comment": [
    "ITEM 5 EDITS AS DATA, NOT PROSE.",
    "",
    "WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The item-5 spec was 68KB of English describing JSON. Three audit rounds",
    "found the same class of defect each time: a correction stated at the top of the document that",
    "never reached the edits it corrected, a new action whose JSON shape was invalid, a runAfter",
    "naming a non-sibling, and a dependency cycle introduced by a correction. Every one of those is a",
    "MECHANICALLY CHECKABLE property expressed in a medium no machine can check. Hand-patching the",
    "prose twice introduced new defects both times.",
    "",
    "So: the edits live here as structured data, check-item5-edits.js validates them, and the readable",
    "spec is GENERATED from this file. A correction then physically cannot fail to propagate, because",
    "there is one source and the prose is output.",
    "",
    "STATE: seeded 2026-07-31 with the CONTENTIOUS edits exactly as the round-2 spec currently states",
    "them — INCLUDING their known defects — so the validator can be seen catching all four auditor",
    "findings before anything is corrected. Fix them here, never in the prose."
  ],
